# Development-only files, not shipped in the packaged .vsix
.vscode/**
**/.git
**/.gitignore
**/*.vsix
**/*.map
testRtl/**
scripts/**
node_modules/.package-lock.json

# The bundled server (server/**) IS shipped: it makes the extension
# self-contained. Exclude only dev-only bits to reduce size.
#
# The real defence against a bloated folder is scripts/bundle-server.js (it
# empties server/ before publishing, then prunes symbols, .playwright and the
# non-host native runtimes). These patterns are the second line of defence: a
# development host whose extension folder grows into the hundreds of MB is
# killed with SIGABRT (exit code 134) right after "Loading development
# extension", before any extension code runs. Keep the folder small.
server/**/*.pdb
server/.playwright/**
server/**/.playwright/**
server/**/*.xml

# icons/** IS shipped: the RTL Hierarchy tree uses the plugin's own SVG
# assets (light + dark variants) so it matches the desktop editor.
